 "category": "Stylize",
 "tags": ["look"],
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "Shoots the picture into a hand tufted rug: the picture is simplified into a handful of yarn colours, each laid as dense cut pile, so every tuft is a soft round tip of fibres that catches the light on one side, and stray fibres blur the line where two yarns meet. Where one colour ends the pile is carved down into a groove the way a tufter trims round each shape, so the shapes stand up like sculpted wool.",
